/* 2026-08-08: In-guide currency converter. toolbar.js appends a sixth pill to #ics-pill-row, "💱 Currency", which expands in place into a two-field converter - US$ and the destination currency, both live inputs, editing either rewrites the other. A reader inside an itinerary converts in both directions: outbound to budget a stop and inbound to read a price off a menu, so a one-way US$-to-local box would have answered half the question. No new data pipeline and no new rate source: the rate is the one Currency-Guide.html already carries, and update_currency_rates.py now emits assets/currency-rates.json (73 currencies, folded country keys) from the same country blocks in the same monthly pass, so the page and the pill cannot quote different numbers. New Brain/scripts/build/build_currency_rates.py does the parse and takes --check for a staleness diff. Country resolution reuses assets/country-guides.json, already sessionStorage-cached under tvecg by the "Also in Country" section, so on a warm tab this costs one extra request rather than two; both sides of the join are folded (lowercase, accents stripped, underscores to spaces) because the Currency-Guide anchors are ASCII with underscores while country-guides.json holds display strings - without the fold Curacao, MALTA, PHILIPPINES and SOUTH AFRICA render no pill at all. Renders nothing when the country is unknown or already on USD (Ecuador, Puerto Rico, Turks and Caicos, United States). Panel is a SIBLING of the pill row, not a child, since that row is flex on desktop and a 2-column grid on mobile and a block child would lay out as another pill in both; the sixth pill also completes the mobile grid, which has sat at five since the Preview Optimized button joined it. Every colour is a theme token and the input is 16px so iOS does not zoom the page on focus. Zero guide HTML changes. Locked by brain_check check_injected_classes_have_css, which now pairs _curFold with its six selectors. toolbar.js -> v228, guide-style.css -> v140. CACHE to v359. */
