/* 2026-08-08: Best-Of-Index cross-category finder (Open Recommendations, content-suggestions-2026-07-16). The 34 Best-of pages were siloed - each answers "the best beaches" or "the best wine regions" and nothing answered "where do I get both". A "Compare categories" disclosure between the search box and the category grid now takes a multi-select of category chips and lists every country present in ALL of them, with that country's real entries under each category, so Beaches + Wine Regions returns Australia (Barossa Valley beside Whitehaven and Bondi), Italy, Portugal, South Africa, Spain and the United States rather than a bare country list. Data is generated, not authored: new Brain/scripts/build/build_best_of_cross.py walks every showcase page listed on the index with balanced-div counting and files each entry under its section-label country, splitting multi-country labels ("Zambia / Zimbabwe") and normalising Antigua/Czechia/DR Congo so the joins line up; Best-Surfing.html is the one page with no section labels, so its country comes from a PLACE_COUNTRY token table applied to each card Google Maps link. A card that resolves to no country is a hard error and the builder writes nothing, because a dropped or mis-attributed entry silently changes which countries intersect. Chip labels are read from the index cards themselves, so the finder always reads like the grid below it. Output is assets/best-of-cross-data.js (window.BEST_OF_CROSS, 34 categories, 1864 country-entries) - a script rather than JSON plus fetch, so the page needs no XHR and still works off disk. CSS went into shared web-travel-style.css as the .bo-x- family, not the page, because check_best_of_css_standard forbids an inline style block on any Best-of page; chips follow the region-filters treatment (glued squared strip on desktop, Form B glued grid on mobile with min-height rather than a fixed 40px, since several labels wrap to three lines at three columns) and Option-B hover. Locked by new brain_check check_best_of_cross_data_fresh, which recomputes from the pages on disk and hard-fails on drift - smoke-tested against fresh, stale-category and missing-file states. Verified in Chromium at 1200px and 393px: 34 chips, correct intersections, zero horizontal overflow, no console errors. web-travel-style.css -> v13. CACHE to v361. */
