/* 2026-08-08: ONE gap constant in the stop card — 12.25px ink-edge to ink-edge from the Read more pill down to the photo (owner rule, after asking more than ten times: "ALL the same from READ MORE TO THE PICTURE ALWAYS"). An eye-level audit of the fleet — items as a reader perceives them, pill/tint/text/image edges rather than DOM rows — found EVERY guide carrying 9-12 different gap values inside its stop cards; the named region alone had six (27.00 prose->pill, 23.00 pill->text, 20.00 pill->band, 12.25 row->row, 6.00 band->text, 21.25 text->photo). Each earlier pass retuned one of the six, which is why the complaint always returned. Ink = what the reader sees as an edge: a text row's ink is its text, 3.125px inside its 15px/1.55 line box; a pill's, a tint's and an image's ink is the box edge — the owner stated this for the hours band explicitly ("measured to the top of the toolbar not words, same from the bottom"). Padding beside a text row supplies 9.125, beside a painted thing the full 12.25. Read more row pb 12->6; card below it pt 8->3.125; card above the photo pb 8->3.125; photo strip pt 10->6; band margins 3->9.125 with 3.125 on the .tve-ph-top/.tve-ph-end first/last-row cases (new .tve-ph-end, stamped in JS). Two REGRESSIONS were caught by measuring rather than reading the CSS, and are why the paddings are non-zero: zeroing the card's padding-bottom let .tour-meet's inner margin-bottom:10px collapse out and reappear as a phantom 10px between card and photo, and .tour-meet's rows keep the base .stop-row margin:10px 0 because the .tour-box > div override reaches direct children only. .tour-meet also loses the 10px VERTICAL padding the mobile block gave it, which contradicted its own locked spec ("renders as just-another-row") and pushed every mobile gap touching it to 22px. Verified by Brain/scripts/gap_audit.py across the fleet: in-scope pairs all read 12.13-12.38 — one value to within an eighth of a pixel. Out of scope by owner instruction: prose -> Read more pill, and the stop header. Locked by new brain_check check_stop_card_gap_constant + contract 8 of check_stop_hours_contract. guide-style.css -> v149, toolbar.js -> v247. CACHE to v386. */
