/* 2026-08-12: toolbar tab dropped a line WHEN CLICKED (owner screenshot). .tb-ddbtn.tb-active swapped the rest state's padding:2px 2px / border:none for padding:4px 12px / border:1.5px, so activating a tab made it 21px WIDER. Between the hamburger breakpoint and 1500px the tab row sits within a few px of the container, so that 21px tipped it: measured in chromium, at 1400px the tab's top moved +30px and the row grew +34px — it literally fell to a second line on click. The 📋 Recommended tab added 2026-08-10 is what pushed the row close enough to the edge for this to show; the reflow itself had always been there. Reserving the space in the rest state was not an option (it widens every tab, ~+220px across the row, forcing a permanent wrap), so the active pill is now drawn with outline + outline-offset:5px, which does not participate in layout. Same outlined look, zero geometry change: re-measured at 1280/1300/1360/1400/1440 — Δ width -1px (the pre-existing font-weight 700→600), Δ tab top 0 everywhere. ITEMS untouched. toolbar.js -> v484. CACHE to v687. */
/* 2026-08-12: dark mode — Trips.html was OPTED OUT of it entirely, and the audit could not see that. Its <body> carried an inline style="background:#f5f4f0;color:#1a1917", which beats every stylesheet rule except !important; the page therefore rendered LIGHT under prefers-color-scheme:dark, and because validate_dark_mode gates its bright-surface check on the page actually being dark, the file passed by never being audited. Two body{...!important} rules existed only to fight that attribute, and removing them in the earlier pill pass left the page half-flipped (9 issues). Fixed at the cause: the inline attribute is gone, so the shared body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--text)} simply works — no !important, and no inline base reset for check_inline_base_reset to flag. That exposed .action-box's hardcoded #fffdf4 cream (a glowing panel on black), now tokenised. Also: shared dark --navy #5a8adb -> #5a9aee — it was 4.26:1 on --surface, under AA, which is why Lounges-US/Europe each carried a page-local override; raising the token fixes every --navy user at once (75 usages) instead. And Cards-ATM's .pill[data-filter=tips] rest-state background, missed when its hover and active states were tokenised. All 13 pages now clean in dark mode; light mode byte-identical before and after. web-travel-style.css -> v44. CACHE to v686. */
/* 2026-08-12: build_climate.py repaired — it had appeared to hang for 20 minutes during the de-versioning pass while in fact working normally, and five defects made that indistinguishable from a deadlock: no argparse at all (so --help fell through to a full 237-city network rebuild — asking the script what it did started an hour of fetching), unflushed stdout (Python block-buffers when piped, so 20 minutes produced 0 bytes), no per-city progress, a cache in /tmp that macOS clears (silently turning an incremental run back into a full refetch), and no way to re-bake the HTML blocks from data already on disk. Now: --bake-only (no network), --city NAME, --force, --cache PATH, flushed per-city progress, cache at ~/.tve-cache/. Also fixes a latent data-loss bug — climate.json was written straight from the partial cache, so any interrupted run could truncate the fleet; out is now seeded from the shipped climate.json (109 cached vs 237 shipped when found) with a backstop that refuses a shorter write. weather.js -> v6 (CLIMATE_GENERATED 2026-08-09 -> 2026-08-12; Rotterdam refetched and confirmed unchanged). CACHE to v685. */
